{
  "id": "euler_number",
  "title": "Euler Number",
  "description": "A dimensionless value used for analyzing fluid flow dynamics problems where the pressure difference between two points is important. The Euler Number measures the ratio of pressure forces to inertial forces.",
  "type": "chart-table",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "# Euler Number Calculator\n\nThe **Euler Number** is a dimensionless value used for analyzing fluid flow dynamics problems where the pressure difference between two points is important.\n\n## Formula\n\n**Eu = dp / (ρ v²)**\n\nWhere:\n- **Eu** = Euler number (dimensionless)\n- **dp** = differential pressure (Pa)\n- **ρ** = density (kg/m³)\n- **v** = fluid flow velocity (m/s)\n\n## Note\nA perfect frictionless flow corresponds to an Euler number equal to 1.\n\n## Pressure Coefficient\n\n**Pressure Coefficient = dp / (½ ρ v²)**"
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "dp",
          "label": "Differential Pressure",
          "unit": "Pa",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 1000
        },
        {
          "id": "rho",
          "label": "Fluid Density",
          "unit": "kg/m³",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 1000
        },
        {
          "id": "v",
          "label": "Fluid Flow Velocity",
          "unit": "m/s",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 5
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "euler_number_result",
          "label": "Euler Number",
          "formula": "inputs.dp / (inputs.rho * inputs.v * inputs.v)",
          "unit": "-"
        },
        {
          "id": "pressure_coefficient",
          "label": "Pressure Coefficient",
          "formula": "inputs.dp / (0.5 * inputs.rho * inputs.v * inputs.v)",
          "unit": "-"
        },
        {
          "id": "dynamic_pressure",
          "label": "Dynamic Pressure",
          "formula": "0.5 * inputs.rho * inputs.v * inputs.v",
          "unit": "Pa"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "datatable",
      "headers": [
        "Parameter",
        "Value",
        "Unit",
        "Description"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Differential Pressure (dp)",
          "inputs.dp",
          "Pa",
          "Pressure difference between two points"
        ],
        [
          "Fluid Density (ρ)",
          "inputs.rho",
          "kg/m³",
          "Density of the fluid"
        ],
        [
          "Fluid Velocity (v)",
          "inputs.v",
          "m/s",
          "Velocity of fluid flow"
        ],
        [
          "Euler Number",
          "inputs.dp / (inputs.rho * inputs.v * inputs.v)",
          "-",
          "Ratio of pressure forces to inertial forces"
        ],
        [
          "Dynamic Pressure",
          "0.5 * inputs.rho * inputs.v * inputs.v",
          "Pa",
          "Kinetic energy per unit volume"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chart",
      "options": {
        "title": {
          "text": "Euler Number vs Velocity"
        },
        "xAxis": {
          "type": "category",
          "name": "Velocity (m/s)"
        },
        "yAxis": {
          "type": "value",
          "name": "Euler Number"
        },
        "series": [
          {
            "data": "generateSeries",
            "type": "line",
            "smooth": true
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}